      "extract": "COLORED JONES POLYNOMIALS WITHOUT TAILS CHRISTINE RUEY SHAN LEE AND ROLAND VAN DER VEEN Abstract. We exhibit an inﬁnite family of knots with the property that the ﬁrst coeﬃcient of the n-colored Jones polynomial grows linearly with n. This shows that the concept of stability and tail seen in the colored Jones polynomials of alternating knots does not generalize naively. 1. Introduction The colored Jones polynomials",
